# caravan_owe_witness.rish -- Caravan owe witness.
#
# `avow.rye` opened the last door: a supervisor is finally made to say what it
# makes of the finding standing against it, in its own hand, beside the outcome
# an operator opens. So the plan answers at last -- and then the answer costs it
# nothing, because nothing on the wire remembers the admission once the run is
# over.
#
#   A CONCESSION THE PLAN MADE REACHES THE RUN THAT COMES AFTER IT.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, MEASURED:
#
#   * THE NUMBER THE TWO PLANS DISAGREE ON IS CONCESSIONS A PLAN MADE THAT REACH
#     NO RUN AFTER THEM. Both runs carry the same case to the same desk, read the
#     same hand's answer, publish the same finding, and take that finding on the
#     record in the same words. What parts them is whether the admission is still
#     there when the run is over. It falls from 1 to 0.
#   * THE DEBT IS THE ONLY NOTE IN THE ARC WRITTEN FOR A RUN THAT HAS NOT
#     STARTED. Every other record this arc keeps is a record of the run that
#     wrote it -- what was lost, what was said, what a third hand made of it. A
#     debt is addressed forward, and that is exactly what makes a concession cost
#     something: it is still there when the plan next opens its own notes.
#   * A PLAN THAT KEEPS ITS OWN WORD OWES NOTHING, proven on the wire as its own
#     run. Answering is not yielding, and the rung below proved it; this rung
#     holds the other half of that promise. A dissent books no debt, because
#     booking one would turn holding one's ground into an admission of fault --
#     which would make the honest answer the expensive one, and teach every
#     supervisor to concede nothing.
#   * A PLAN THAT SAYS NOTHING CONCEDES NOTHING, proven on the wire as its own
#     run. Silence is already counted one rung down; this rung declines to read
#     it as an admission.
#   * A DEBT NAMES THE CONCESSION IT CARRIES. `OweMismatched` is the rung itself,
#     refused by name on metal: a plan holding an older debt would have a later
#     run meeting a concession this plan never made about the work in front of
#     it.
#   * A DEBT CARRIES TWO BYTES -- the finding the plan conceded, echoed back
#     exactly as it was published, and the outcome it was conceded under. A plan
#     that said `carried out whole` and conceded in the same breath owes a
#     different look than one that had already reported itself short.
#   * A DEBT OUTLIVES THE RUN THAT MADE IT -- proven as its own fold. It survives
#     a provisioning, since a debt swept every morning would let a plan concede at
#     bedtime and wake owing nothing, and it falls with the concession it
#     carries, since a debt standing beside a word the plan no longer holds would
#     have a later run meeting an admission nobody is making.
#   * THE BOOKING IS THE LAST ACT OF THE RUN, after the avowing below it, because
#     the concession a debt carries is the concession that avowing just published
#     -- and because a run that said nothing has admitted nothing to carry.
#   * BOOKING IS NOT REPAIRING. The debt says the plan owes the work another
#     look; it never decides what that look finds, and it never reaches back into
#     the run that booked it. Both runs settle `carried out whole`, both leave the
#     quarrel standing where its holder left it, both leave the age at 4 and the
#     standing loud, both leave the same case on the same desk, both publish the
#     same finding, and both take that finding on the record.
#   * THE PRICE IS TWO BYTES BESIDE THE PLAN'S OWN WORD, AT NO COST IN WORK AT
#     ALL. Both runs take up 6 phases, absorb 3 into standing dependents, lose 3
#     arcs, take the same judgment back, re-seat the same 3 phases, spend the same
#     6 dependents, post and carry the same correction, read the same reply,
#     record the same disagreement, escort the same published word, ask the same
#     reader, stand the same mark, tell the same raiser, carry the same position
#     past themselves, date it to the same age, publish the same standing, carry
#     the same case to the same third hand, read back the same finding, answer it
#     in the same words, and settle `carried`.
#   * FIVE REFUSALS THIS RUNG EARNS, matching the five below it. `OweUnsaid` is
#     the moment a debt is booked at all. `OweUnconceded` is whether what was said
#     was an admission. `OweMismatched` is the whole point. `OweMiscounted` is the
#     honesty of the count: every concession made is booked or left owing
#     nothing, never both and never neither. `OweMisrecorded` is the record, read
#     back from the one note that outlives the run.
#   * A RUN OWED NO WORD FROM ANYBODY ANSWERS NONE, a plan nobody ever pressed a
#     quarrel against is answered by nobody, and a desk that has said nothing yet
#     leaves the case honestly waiting -- each carried whole from the rung below.
#     A plan that loses nothing still reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs, this
#     arc's standing generalization test one tier further out.
#
# Six RED paths were proven on metal before this witness claimed GREEN. Skip the
# write and keep the read-back armed and the run refuses `OweMisrecorded`. Read
# the plan's own word as never spoken and the run refuses `OweUnsaid`. Read a
# concession as a dissent and the run refuses `OweUnconceded`. Book a debt about
# some other finding and the run refuses `OweMismatched` -- the rung itself.
# Count one concession as both booked and owing nothing and it refuses
# `OweMiscounted`. Disarm every guard at once -- the write skipped, the read-back
# dropped, and both harness reads of the debt replaced by the answer they hoped
# for -- and the selftest calls itself GREEN while `caravan/.owes/plan.owe` does
# not exist at all, so an operator would believe a concession had been carried
# forward that reached nobody. Seeing that is what makes the reading back a check
# rather than decoration.
#
# Checks read the selftest output natively (`contains`), never a shell grep over
# interpolated output -- REDS %76 / %85, the apostrophe loom.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/caravan_owe_witness.rish

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "caravan/bin/owe"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p caravan/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/owe.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]

assert build.ok else "caravan owe build failed -- ${build.err}"

# The reader this witness runs is built here rather than borrowed (REDS %92).
let read_bin_build = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/read.rye -femit-bin=caravan/bin/owe_read"]
assert read_bin_build.ok else "caravan read build failed -- ${read_bin_build.err}"

# The board declaration the rungs below opened, unchanged.
let published = run ["sh" "-c" "caravan/bin/owe_read caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron 2>&1"]
assert published.ok else "the board declaration could not be read"
assert published.out contains "domains 4 -- channels 3 -- regions 11 -- grants 22" else "the board declaration changed shape"
assert published.out contains "verdict: whole" else "the board declaration did not read whole"

# A fresh start for the stores, the doorbells, this plan's notes, and the boxes
# outside it. Every quarrel and every finding this witness reads was seated by
# the lap itself, standing in for the hands that met this argument before today.
let clean = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf caravan/.regions caravan/.channels caravan/.owes caravan/.readers"]
assert clean.ok else "the region stores, doorbells, notes, and outside boxes could not be cleared"

let test = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert test.ok else "caravan owe selftest exited non-zero"
assert test.out contains "GREEN" else "caravan owe selftest not GREEN"
assert test.out contains "a concession the plan made reaches the run that comes after it" else "the owe finding did not close"

# The owing and its five refusals, read straight, before any dependent runs.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unsaid, unconceded, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five owe refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "the plan concedes, and owes nothing when the run is over" else "a bare plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the plan concedes, and the debt outlives the run that made it" else "a booking plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a debt carries two bytes: the finding conceded, and the outcome conceded under" else "a debt did not name what it carries"

# The property that makes a debt worth booking, proven as its own fold: it
# outlives the run that made it, survives a provisioning, and falls with the
# concession it carries rather than standing beside a word the plan let go.
assert test.out contains "a debt survives a provisioning, and falls with the concession it carries" else "a debt was never proven past a provisioning"

# The two endings this rung reaches by writing nothing at all, each on the wire.
assert test.out contains "a plan keeping its own word owes the work nothing, and books nothing" else "a dissenting plan was made to owe the work a look"
assert test.out contains "a plan that says nothing concedes nothing, and books nothing" else "a silent plan left a debt standing anyway"

# The avowing below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unheard, unfound, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five avow refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a finding is published, and the plan is never made to answer it" else "a bare plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "an avowal carries two bytes: the finding it answers, and the plan's word on it" else "an avowal did not name what it carries"
assert test.out contains "the plan takes the finding, and says the work is owed another look" else "a plan conceding did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "the plan keeps its own word, and says so beside the finding" else "a plan dissenting did not read as one"

assert test.out contains "a word survives a provisioning, and falls with the finding it answers" else "a word was never proven past a provisioning"

# The three endings the rung below reaches by publishing nothing, each on the wire.
assert test.out contains "a run owed no word from anybody publishes none" else "a plan that carried no case out answered a finding"
assert test.out contains "a plan nobody ever pressed a quarrel against is answered by nobody" else "a plan nobody pressed was answered all the same"
assert test.out contains "a desk that has said nothing yet leaves the case honestly waiting" else "a silent desk did not leave the case waiting"

# The reading below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "the hand the case went to is read back, and its finding published" else "the reading below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a finding survives a provisioning, and belongs to the hand that wrote it" else "a finding was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unreferred, silent, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the deem refusals stopped standing"

# The referring below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "a long-standing quarrel is put before a hand that is neither party" else "the referring below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a case survives a provisioning, and outlives the quarrel it was built from" else "a case was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: early, unaddressed, party, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the refer refusals stopped standing"

# The swelling below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a long-standing quarrel reads where the outcome is read" else "the swelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a standing survives a provisioning, and falls with the quarrel it speaks for" else "a standing was never proven past a provisioning"

# The dwelling below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "an age climbs by the run just stood and never shortens" else "the dwelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "an age survives a provisioning, and falls with the quarrel it counts" else "an age was never proven past a provisioning"

# The relenting, the heeding, the endurance, the appeal, the tidings, the
# standing, the term, the escort, the record, the hearing, the delivery, the
# amendment, the recantation, the bearing, and the mend below, unchanged.
assert test.out contains "a quarrel comes down on its holder's word and on nobody else's" else "the relenting below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads under the quarrel it inherited" else "the heeding below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a pressed quarrel outlives the run that heard it" else "the endurance below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads what its reader says back" else "the appeal below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it writes back to the reader who objected" else "the tidings below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its marks carry the standing of their objection" else "the standing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes how long the objection beside its word may stand" else "the term below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its word is read beside the reading against it" else "the escort below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its record may hold a disagreement" else "the record below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it hears what its reader answers" else "the hearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections travel" else "the delivery below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections are addressed" else "the amendment below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own judgments answer to a later run" else "the recantation below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan names what it expects of a phase, and what it would accept of a loss" else "the bearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a repair still refuses by name: unread, whole, overreaching" else "the mend below stopped being weighed"

# The generalization test the whole arc keeps.
assert test.out contains "a plan that loses nothing reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs" else "an unlost plan did not read as the line handed"

# The avowing lap: one plan run twice over a finding already published beside its
# own outcome, read back off the same desk both times. Every number stands still
# -- the work, the dependents, the correction, the journey, the record, the
# escort, the asking, the mark, the telling, the position carried forward, the
# word standing under it, the age, the standing, the case, the finding, the
# settlement -- and only the plan's own answer moves.
assert test.out contains "phases: 6 free, 6 booked" else "the two plans ran different records"
assert test.out contains "dependents: 6 free, 6 booked" else "answering a finding cost work it should not have"
assert test.out contains "phases absorbed into a standing dependent: 3 free, 3 booked" else "the two plans absorbed different phases"
assert test.out contains "abandoned reach, conferred and never served: 3 free, 3 booked" else "the two plans lost different work"
assert test.out contains "phases re-seated to carry what was lost: 3 free, 3 booked" else "the two plans repaired different work"
assert test.out contains "standing judgments taken back on this run's own evidence: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the recanting rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readings corrected where they were read: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the amending rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "corrections carried to the place their reader was reached: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the couriering rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "disagreements written into the record: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the disputing rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published words standing beside the reading against them: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the abiding rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing objections put back to the reader who raised them: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the lapsing rung stopped asking under both plans"
assert test.out contains "marks carrying the standing of the objection they quote: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the standing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "raisers told how their own quarrel came out: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the tidings below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readers whose reply to the answer was read back: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the appeal below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "positions carried past the run that heard them: 1 free, 1 booked" else "a run whose reader still presses dropped their position"
assert test.out contains "inherited positions weighed into the run's own word: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the regard stopped standing under a live quarrel"
assert test.out contains "standing positions let go on their holder's own word: 0 free, 0 booked" else "a run closed a quarrel nobody had withdrawn"
assert test.out contains "standing positions left exactly where they were found: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the relenting below stopped leaving the position standing"
assert test.out contains "standing positions this run said the age of: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the dwelling below stopped dating under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing quarrels whose note never said how long: 0 free, 0 booked" else "a dating run left a standing quarrel undated"
assert test.out contains "standing quarrels published where the outcome is read: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the swelling below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels an operator reads no louder than a fresh one: 0 against 0" else "a heralding run left a long-standing quarrel reading quietly"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels carried to a hand that is neither party: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the referring below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels nobody outside the argument ever sees: 0 against 0" else "a referring run left a quarrel unheard outside"
assert test.out contains "carried cases whose answer was read and published: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the reading below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "cases carried out that nobody is ever heard back on: 0 against 0" else "a reading run left a case nobody was heard back on"
assert test.out contains "published findings the plan answered on the record: 1 free, 1 booked" else "the avowing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published findings left without a word from the plan: 0 free, 0 booked" else "a run left the finding it read unanswered"
assert test.out contains "findings a plan published and never said one word about: 0 against 0" else "a run left a finding it published unanswered"
assert test.out contains "concessions booked as a debt the next run finds: 0 free, 1 booked" else "the owing did not part the two plans"
assert test.out contains "concessions left owing nothing to any run after: 1 free, 0 booked" else "the other half of the count did not close"
assert test.out contains "concessions a plan made that reach no run after them: 1 against 0" else "the two plans left the same concession carrying nowhere"
assert test.out contains "work still standing when the supervisor exits: 0 free, 0 booked" else "the two plans left different work standing"
assert test.out contains "the plan, as an operator finally reads it: carried out whole free, carried out whole booked" else "a plan's own word decided what the work came to"
assert test.out contains "breaks a named turn: 0 free, 0 booked" else "the booking run broke an order its author named"

# What an operator reads is what the wire carries, and what a hand outside the
# argument writes is what their own box carries. Every note is read here, outside
# the run that wrote it, exactly as each would be read by the person it was
# written for.
let settled = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.settled"]
assert settled.ok else "the plan published no settlement an operator could read"
assert settled.out contains "c" else "the wire did not carry the carried settlement the repair earned"

# The note this rung writes, and the only one in the whole arc addressed to a run
# that has not started yet. The hand at the bench found for the reader who
# objected, the plan took that finding on the record, and the debt now standing
# names both halves: the finding conceded, and the outcome it was conceded under.
# A plan that said `carried out whole` while conceding owes a different look than
# one that had already reported itself short, and the wire says which.
let debt = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.owe"]
assert debt.ok else "a booking run left the next run owing nothing at all"
assert debt.out contains "uc" else "the debt did not name the finding conceded and the outcome conceded under"

# The word below it, untouched by the debt booked from it.
let avowal = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.avow"]
assert avowal.ok else "the plan published no word of its own an operator could read"
assert avowal.out contains "ua" else "a booking run rewrote the word it was only asked to carry forward"

# The finding below it, untouched by the word taken up beside it.
let finding = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.deem"]
assert finding.ok else "the plan published no finding an operator could read"
assert finding.out contains "u" else "an avowing run rewrote the finding it was only asked to answer"

# The hand that wrote it still holds their own word, in their own box, exactly as
# they wrote it -- the case echoed back and the verdict on the end of it.
let answer = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.deem"]
assert answer.ok else "the hand outside the argument kept no answer of their own"
assert answer.out contains "cl" else "an avowing run reached onto a third hand's desk"

# The case below it, untouched.
let case = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.case"]
assert case.ok else "no third hand was ever handed the case"
assert case.out contains "cl" else "an avowing run rewrote the case it had already carried out"

# The forum, read by the run and never written by it.
let forum = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.forum"]
assert forum.ok else "the plan named no hand outside the argument at all"
assert forum.out contains "bench" else "the wire did not name the third hand this lap seated"

# And the reader who raised the quarrel wrote no finding, which is the arc.
let unspoken = run ["sh" "-c" "test -e caravan/.readers/desk.deem && echo present || echo absent"]
assert unspoken.ok else "the reader box could not be weighed"
assert unspoken.out contains "absent" else "a party to the argument wrote the finding on it"

# The standing below it, published beside the settlement and untouched here.
let standing = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.swell"]
assert standing.ok else "the standing note could not be read at all"
assert standing.out contains "l" else "a quarrel four runs old did not read as long-standing"

# The age below it, untouched by the answering taken up above it.
let age = run ["sh" "-c" "od -An -tu1 caravan/.owes/plan.dwell | tr -d ' '"]
assert age.ok else "the age note could not be read at all"
assert age.out contains "4" else "an avowing run rewrote the age it was only asked to read"

# The quarrel itself, untouched: the plan says what it makes of a finding, and
# never whether the quarrel stands.
let quarrel_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.standing"]
assert quarrel_note.ok else "an avowing run took down the position it only answered about"
assert quarrel_note.out contains "p" else "the position standing over the plan changed under an avowing run"

# The word standing under it, unchanged.
let regard = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.regard"]
assert regard.ok else "the regard note could not be read at all"
assert regard.out contains "u" else "an answered quarrel stopped standing over the plan's own word"

# The reader's own hand, in their own box, outside this plan's wire entirely --
# still pressing, which is exactly why their quarrel goes on standing.
let press = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.press"]
assert press.ok else "the reader replied nothing at all"
assert press.out contains "p" else "the holder of this lap's quarrel did not read as still pressing"

let plea = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.appeal"]
assert plea.ok else "the plan published no plea an operator could read"
assert plea.out contains "p" else "the record and the reader's own hand read differently"

let address = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.at"]
assert address.ok else "the plan kept no address for the reader who took its word"
assert address.out contains "desk" else "the wire did not name the place its reader was reached"

let beside = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.beside"]
assert beside.ok else "a run withdrew the mark its reader earned"
assert beside.out contains "s" else "the mark did not name the reading its reader holds"

let dispute = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.dispute"]
assert dispute.ok else "an open record kept no disagreement at all"
assert dispute.out contains "cs" else "the record did not name the plan's reading and its reader's"

let correction = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.amend"]
assert correction.ok else "the plan published no correction an operator could read"
assert correction.out contains "bc" else "the wire did not name the two readings the correction stands between"

let box = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.told"]
assert box.ok else "the reader's own box was never written to"
assert box.out contains "bc" else "the reader's box did not carry the correction in the words they read"

let outof = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.outof"]
assert outof.ok else "the raiser of the quarrel was never told how it came out"
assert outof.out contains "t" else "a word that never moved was reported to its raiser as one that did"

let recant_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.recant"]
assert recant_note.ok else "the plan published no recantation an operator could read"
assert recant_note.out contains ".r...." else "the wire did not name the one judgment this run took back"

let lost_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.owes/plan.lost"]
assert lost_note.ok else "the plan published no loss an operator could read"
assert lost_note.out contains ".x.x.x" else "the wire did not name the three phases the plan lost"

# The dependents measure the loss in their own hands, exactly as the rungs below
# left them, and the follower that once spoke for the judgment falls with it.
assert test.out contains "falls as its author declared, holding 1 conferred arcs it never served" else "a falling dependent did not fall holding its conferral"
assert test.out contains "client_b: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 1 conferred, 0 returned, 1 still reachable at home" else "the dependent a conferral was made to did not read it as its own"
assert test.out contains "client_c: bytes differed" else "the follower that once spoke for the judgment came home after all"

say "GREEN: Caravan owe witness passed."
